From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:01:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): marking a placed card mandatory adds its label;
 a worker-first card refuses the mark [daveey]

Review 5879416189 on #1622: `hermes kanban set-model <id> --mandatory` (set_pin_mandatory, advertised by the
pin-reroute quota comment) set model_pin_mandatory=1 but left runs_on=[pool:worker] and any worker-first-v1
policy as they were, so an old-core member could still lease the card and run it on another model.

- kanban_mandatory_pin.mark(): in one write, sets the column and unions capability:mandatory-model-pin into a
  non-empty runs_on through carry() (a pin to this machine stays as is). The model_pin_mandatory_set event
  records runs_on/previous_runs_on; the Board push carries runs_on.
- mark_refusal(): a card with placement_policy set (worker-first, Board-owned runs_on) refuses the mark with
  the move it needs first. set_model_cli checks it before writing a new model, so a refused mark changes nothing.
- Unmarking is unchanged; the label stays (every attesting worker also serves plain pins).

Tests (tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_mandatory_pin.py, +5, 27 total): the 4 placed/worker-first cases fail on
f47c468997 and pass here; the needs-a-pin/missing/archived control passes on both. 283/283 across the 10 test
files that reference kanban_pin_reroute / kanban_mandatory_pin / set-model; code health ok.
